..careful connecting: Connection name: anything you like, e.g. sql_course.
Connection group: leave blank.
Connect using: choose Server and Port.
Server Address: localhost (or 127.0.0.1) if Postgres runs on your own computer.
Port: 5432, the Postgres default. If you installed more than one Postgres version or use Docker, it may be 5433 or another port. Use the same port you used in the other window.
Database: sql_course. This is the key field. Your current connection uses postgres, which is why the tables look gone.
Username: usually postgres unless you created a different role.
Use password: pick Ask on connect (or Save as plaintext, which is convenient but stored unencrypted in your settings). Enter the password you set when installing Postgres.

